  "summary": "Overnight sentiment stayed defensive as October\u2019s hotter-than-expected CPI and hawkish Fed rhetoric kept December rate-hike pricing firm, pressuring Treasuries and supporting the dollar narrative in the headline flow. Frozen marks still show elevated crude\u2014WTI near $86.53 and Brent near $92.76\u2014with gold around $4,000.50, while U.S. benchmarks sit at roughly 7,521 on the S&P 500, 25,466 on the Nasdaq, and 52,486 on the Dow amid a sub-20 VIX. Chicago Fed President Goolsbee called the inflation report \u201cborderline disturbing,\u201d reinforcing fears of a larger hike, while Williams argued the Fed should gather more information on price risks. Energy headlines highlighted jet-fuel pain and Gulf routing shifts as oil import patterns adjust. Watch for the next U.S. inflation and housing prints, further Fedspeak, and whether high crude prices broaden into corporate margins; official BoC framework language and dated Fed operational remarks offer little near-term policy offset.",
